---
// Accessibility statement (Barrierefreiheit). Built 26 Oct 2026 after a check of every page:
// keyboard only, 200% and 400% zoom, reduced motion, text spacing, and checks of headings,
// labels, text alternatives, target sizes and colour contrast.
// ONLY write here what is really true today. When a limitation below is fixed, remove it;
// when something new is checked (e.g. the screen reader test with NVDA), add it.
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { owner } from "../data/owner.js";

const email = owner.emails[0];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  lead="Cave Wear should work for everyone – with a mouse, a keyboard or a screen reader. Our aim is the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2, level AA."
  description="How the Cave Wear website is built to be accessible, what we check and where it isn't there yet."
>
  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Everything can be used with the keyboard alone. A visible ring shows where you are.</li>
    <li>A "Skip to content" link at the start of every page jumps past the navigation.</li>
    <li>
      Every page has a clear structure: headings in order and landmarks for the header,
      navigation, main content and footer.
    </li>
    <li>Product photos have text descriptions. Decorative graphics are hidden from screen readers.</li>
    <li>Form fields have labels, and form messages are read out by screen readers.</li>
    <li>If your system asks for reduced motion, animations and smooth scrolling are switched off.</li>
    <li>The site stays usable at 200% zoom and with larger letter and line spacing.</li>
    <li>No pop-ups, no time limits, no cookies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we check it</h2>
  <p>
    Every page is tested with the keyboard only, at 200% and 400% zoom, with reduced motion and
    with larger text spacing. Headings, labels, text descriptions, the size of clickable areas and
    colour contrast are checked as well.
  </p>

  <h2>Known limitations</h2>
  <ul>
    <!-- Remove when the mobile phase is done -->
    <li>
      The site is designed for desktop first. On phones and at 400% zoom, the header doesn't fit
      the screen yet – the mobile layout is still being finished.
    </li>
    <!-- Remove when the header contrast over the top photos is fixed -->
    <li>
      On the photos at the top of the Home and Products pages, the navigation is hard to read until
      you scroll down a little.
    </li>
    <!-- Remove when the hero text can also be shown without a mouse -->
    <li>
      The short texts on the Home photo appear when you move the mouse over it. Screen readers read
      them, but with the keyboard alone they can't be seen yet.
    </li>
    <!-- Remove when the product page explains why "Add to pack" is switched off -->
    <li>
      On product pages, "Add to pack" stays switched off until you choose a size. There is no note
      yet that says so.
    </li>
    <!-- Remove when the photo viewer can be moved with the keyboard and by touch -->
    <li>
      In the photo viewer, a zoomed photo can only be moved around with a mouse. Swiping and
      pinching on touch screens will come with the mobile version.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Feedback</h2>
  <p>
    Did something not work for you? Write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> or use the{" "}
    <a href="/contact#contact-form">contact form</a>. We'll answer, and if you need it, we'll send
    you the content in a form that works for you.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
